          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If a note says \"use additional code\", is that optional?",
          "answer": "When a note indicates \"use additional code,\" it often means that the additional code clarifies or provides more specificity about the condition being documented. However, whether this is optional or mandatory can depend on the context of the coding guidelines.\n\nAccording to ICD-10 coding conventions, \"use additional code\" is typically associated with a need for more detailed information about a specific condition. In many cases, it is not optional if the additional code is necessary to fully capture the patient's clinical picture. In other circumstances, if the additional details are not critical for reporting or do not change the management of the patient, it might be treated as optional.\n\nFor precise coding, it's crucial to follow the established conventions and guidelines, as they are tailored to ensure clear and complete documentation. If there's uncertainty about whether to use an additional code, consulting relevant coding manuals or guidelines can provide clarity.\n\nFor more information on coding conventions, see the document \"ICD-10-CM code structure and the conventions that govern selection.\"\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
